{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["And he loved also Rachel — 'And also' means a more complete love, that is: he came to her and also loved her. Most instances of 'also' in the Torah function thus. So too: וברכתם גם אותי — 'also you shall bless me.' And so too: גם אותך הרגתי — 'I would still have killed you.' Here too: הנה לחצתי רגליך ונעשית שפי ופסח — even so, still."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The last two examples are cited in compressed form; the second appears to conflate multiple verses or carry a textual difficulty. Rendered hyper-literally as the Hebrew stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:40.864913964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}